<h3>Application Areas</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Industrial air treatment</strong>: Bag air filters are commonly used in industrial environments such as factories and workshops to remove dust, particles, chemical gases and odors from the air to ensure a clean production environment, improve work efficiency, and protect production equipment.</li>
<li><strong>Commercial buildings</strong>: In commercial office buildings, hotels, shopping malls and other places, bag air filters are used in central air conditioning systems to filter dust, pollen, mold and bacteria in the air and provide clean and healthy indoor air.</li>
<li><strong>Healthcare facilities</strong>: In places such as hospitals, laboratories and pharmaceutical plants, bag air filters are used in sensitive environments such as clean rooms, operating rooms and laboratories to ensure that the air is free of bacteria, viruses and other contaminants.</li>
<li><strong>Electronics industry</strong>: In the semiconductor manufacturing and electronic assembly processes, bag air filters are used to remove tiny particles in the air to ensure the cleanliness of the production process and avoid damage to electronic components by tiny particles.</li>
<li><strong>Food and beverage manufacturing</strong>: During food and beverage processing, bag air filters are used to keep the production environment clean, prevent dust, bacteria and other contaminants from entering the product, and ensure product safety and quality.</li>
<li><strong>Energy industry</strong>: In energy production fields such as power plants and petrochemical plants, bag air filters are used to remove particulate matter produced during the combustion process and reduce air pollution.</li>
</ul>
